# VATM VVTS + VVLT combined scenario - 52 movements/hour
# Split after adjustment: VVTS ~60.60% and VVLT ~39.40% (rounded to whole movements: VVTS 32, VVLT 20).
# Allocation rule: VVLT receives foreign-carrier international flights and Vietnamese-carrier international flights with stage length >= 1000 km.
# VVTS keeps domestic flows plus Vietnamese-carrier short-haul exceptions below 1000 km (Bangkok/Cambodia/Laos/Phuket/Sanya/Langkawi group).
# Flow emphasis: VVLT concentrated East/Southeast and South/Southwest; VVTS remains North/Northeast-dominant from domestic North-Central demand.
# RWY assumption: VVTS 25L departures / 25R arrivals; VVLT RNP RWY 23L SID/STAR procedures.
# Decision-support / Non-operational. Use only for simulation validation.
# TEST MODIFICATION: Generic conflict alert/protected-zone horizontal threshold set to 3 NM.
# TEST REQUIREMENT: Wake separation check HEAVY departure vs MEDIUM landing = 6 NM.
# NOTE: BlueSky ZONER applies a global protected-zone radius; pair-specific wake separation requires WebFTS/STCA rule layer support.
00:00:00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00>ASAS ON
00:00:00>ZONER 3
00:00:00>ZONEDH 1000
00:00:00>RSZONER 3
00:00:00>RSZONEDH 1000
00:00:00>DTLOOK 300
00:00:00>ECHO VATM TEST: Generic ASAS/STCA protected-zone horizontal separation = 3 NM, vertical = 1000 ft. Wake-sep rule to verify in WebFTS: HEAVY departure vs MEDIUM arrival = 6 NM.
